WEBVTT

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.040
That's a new record, May-<i>chan</i>!

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:20.080
What are you doing, Maple?

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.200
That's very childish.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.700
Hey, Nuts, it's normal to start washing
from the top of your body.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.700
Huh? Starting from the bottom is normal.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.620
Thank you for your purchase!

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.790
The total comes out to 1,520 yen.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:51.000
Thank you! We look forward
to seeing you again.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.330
--Ugh...
--Ouch...

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.750
Hey, Nuts! Watch where you're going!

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:05.370
I couldn't help it--
I didn't see you there, Azuki.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:09.620
What?! Who are you calling
too tiny to be visible?!

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.580
I didn't go that far!

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.290
Another day, another fight...

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.410
They're always so full of energy!

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:16.950
What, you want some?!

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.700
Fine! Come get some!

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:59.330
Jeez, I had a rough day today
thanks to Nuts.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.750
That wasn't all my fault!

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.620
No, it was!

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:06.700
Stop it, both of you. We're eating.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.000
Where did I fail to discipline them?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.750
Don't they get tired of
doing that every single day?

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:23.290
Nuts-<i>chan </i>used to be all over Azuki,
calling her "Big Sister" and all that.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.200
Azuki can be so childish sometimes.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.410
Is that really how the eldest cat
is supposed to act?

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.580
What are you doing, Nuts?

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.950
It's not your turn to do the dishes today.
Stop going out of your way.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:45.080
What kind of attitude is that?
I'm the one helping here.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.660
Huh. You're actually doing a pretty good job.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:54.080
I know right? Yeah!

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.580
Even I can do at least some...

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:00.250
We all knew that was coming.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.330
Wait-- Hey! That's my bowl!

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.620
Oh, I'm sorry... I'll clean up right away...

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.950
Hey, idiot! Don't touch that!

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.200
I'll do it! Just stay back!

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.450
C-Come on!

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.700
You didn't have to say it like that!

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.450
What's her issue?

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.620
These ribbons are all tangled up!

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.950
This is heavy...

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.450
Maybe I got too much for one go...

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:47.370
Ouch!

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.000
What are you doing?!

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.250
N-No, what are you doing?!

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.330
--Why are you even there?
--Azuki and Coconut seem
to be more tangled up this time.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:56.580
--You're the one that bumped into me!
--Azuki and Coconut seem
to be more tangled up this time.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.660
--Why would you not move when someone
carrying a ton of stuff walks by?!
--Tangled up?

00:04:58.660 --> 00:04:59.830
--Why would you not move when someone
carrying a ton of stuff walks by?!
--Tangled up means...

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.830
--Maybe if you weren't carrying
so much stuff while being so small,
--Tangled up means...

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:02.870
--Maybe if you weren't carrying
so much stuff while being so small,
--...to end up like this!

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.580
--this wouldn't have happened!
--...to end up like this!

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:07.500
--No, it's your fault for being inconsiderate!
--Oh, clumsy Chocola is so cute as well...

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.660
--No, it's your fault for being
outside my field of vision!
--Oh, clumsy Chocola is so cute as well...

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:10.410
--No, it's your fault for being
outside my field of vision!
--Maybe Azuki and Coconut need to just

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.580
--Enough already!
--Maybe Azuki and Coconut need to just

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.580
go all the way with this for once.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:21.830
That could be a good idea.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:28.080
Azuki, Coconut, if you want to fight,
just fight as much as you want.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.120
In fact, with full force.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.500
But no violence.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.750
Huh?

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.200
You two will go head to head,
but in a sportsmanlike manner.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:44.620
And that is how the battle began.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.790
"Minaduki House Cup"
"Team Coconut vs Team Azuki"

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.500
Here, I declare the start
of Minaduki House Cup,

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.160
the battle between
Team Azuki and Team Coconut!

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:06.160
White side: Azuki, Cinnamon, Vanilla!

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.410
Facing off against...

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:12.910
Coconut, Maple, Chocola!

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.910
Sounds like fun!

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:18.540
Why us, too?

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.910
Don't think too deeply about this.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:22.870
Please don't make it hurt...

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:27.950
I don't even have to show
my true powers! I'll beat you easily!

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:32.200
I'm the one that's easily going
to take you down and knock you out!

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:51.540
And the first game is... this!

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:54.120
Twister!

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:58.200
The contestants are Coconut from
the red team and Azuki from the white team.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:04.040
First, Coconut, right hand to blue!

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.790
Azuki, right foot to yellow!

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:15.370
Next, Coconut, left foot to red!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.160
Azuki, left hand to green!

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:21.450
You put your hand or foot on where
the spinning thing stops.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:26.870
If your body touches anywhere
else on the mat, you lose.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:31.540
It's hard to deny Nuts-<i>chan</i>'s advantage here...

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:34.160
The difference in reach is quite big.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:37.870
What...?! Don't underestimate me, you idiots!

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.580
I-I can... do this...

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:46.790
Stop... It tickles...

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.330
H-Hey, Azuki.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.160
That's not fair...

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.830
Hey, what's wrong with you?!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.250
Who's fault do you think it is?!

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.410
The next is this match-up!

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:06.200
Th-This is...

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:10.790
Super high-class cat food,
costing at least 1,000 yen per can!

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:14.040
Yes! Yes! Chocola will do this!

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:16.790
Speed or volume, I'm ready to compete!

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:18.200
Me, too!

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.660
I want to do this, too! Come on!

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.700
You all just want to eat!

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.040
Okay, enough.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.120
Let's decide by lottery.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.370
Yay!

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:34.250
We are definitely on the winning side.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:37.580
What, so we're the underdogs?

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.200
But we're cats.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.000
Jeez, that's no fun.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.160
Boo.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:47.000
And now, the food-resisting
contest starts, now!

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.950
Oh, this is rough...

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.870
I wouldn't last ten seconds...

00:08:57.410 --> 00:09:00.660
Next is, guess what's in the box--

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.750
What?

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:09.200
This cardboard box fits so well,
it's irresistible!

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.620
They lost to their instincts before
the fight even began...

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.870
Next, spoon relay!

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:20.830
If you drop the ping pong ball
on the spoon, you lose.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.040
Ready...

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.290
Go, Maple-<i>chan</i>! Burn rubber!

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.790
Fight on, Cinnamon!

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.950
Maple! Over here! Over here!

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:38.500
Chocola has no idea what they're saying.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:43.200
I get the feeling it's something dumb.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.870
Who're you calling dumb?!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.000
Oh.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.540
Yes! I did it!

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:51.000
--Oh.
--Both of you are disqualified.

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:02.450
From the east, Cinnamon No Sato.

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:07.410
From the west, Chocola No Yama.

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:10.790
Ready? Ready?

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:21.250
Go!

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:28.410
Cinnamon's hips are amazing!

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:31.250
One bad move, and Chocola
will be bounced out of the ring!

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:35.870
But Chocola won't give up!

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.250
The difference in power is clear.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:46.000
It's like Cinnamon's hips are peaches,
but Chocola's are plums.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:51.080
Chocola's plums are supple
and not to be underestimated!

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.450
Peaches and plums...?

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:57.870
Oh, the peaches and plums
are mashing together...

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:04.200
Oh no, I'm getting moist!

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.660
Oh.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.660
Chocola No Yama wins!

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:16.040
From the east, Vanilla No Umi.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:20.830
From the west, Chiyo Coconut.

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:23.330
Do it! Crush her!

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:24.870
Gotcha.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:27.950
Coconut has the obvious size advantage...

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:30.500
Does Vanilla have a secret plan?

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.540
Go! Vanilla!

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:36.500
Don't let your guard down Coconut!

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:39.580
Go!

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:46.790
Pardon the interruption. Here is a riddle.

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:49.450
A r-riddle?

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.790
"Palmate" is a word meaning
having a shape similar to a hand.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:57.000
What do you call a person shaped like a hip?

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.040
What?!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:01.750
Come on, what is it? What's the answer?

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:06.080
What? A person who looks like a hip?

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.330
Come on, come on. What is it? Think.

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:12.370
While Nuts-<i>chan </i>is wracking her brain,
Vanilla is attacking relentlessly.

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:14.200
Come on, what is it? Come on.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:17.370
Vanilla is always the scheming one...

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:18.950
What's the answer?!

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:25.160
I get it! Hip sumo wrestler!

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.910
The answer is: a hipster.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.790
Vanilla No Umi wins!

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:42.450
From the east, Azuki Zakari.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:47.330
From the west, Maple Nishiki.

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:50.080
Ready, ready.

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.330
Go!

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:56.700
This is a good match.

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.750
Not bad, Maplez!

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:04.910
I'll show her!

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.660
Azu-<i>nyan </i>is unleashing a blazing fast combo!

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.700
The movement of her hips...

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:20.750
It's like the move invented by former
boxing champion Jack Dempsey,

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.540
the Dempsey Roll!

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:27.870
By weaving her body to the sides,
her blows are both powerful and rapid!

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:29.910
I've got this!

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:37.790
Now I will launch an uppercut from
this low position and finish this!

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:44.080
Maple Nishiki wins!

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:48.910
Coco-<i>chan </i>and Azu-<i>nyan </i>lost
in really similar ways!

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:50.750
The two are really similar.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:52.830
Dammit!

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:59.410
Umm... So what were we competing about?

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:03.160
It all started as a fight
between Azuki and Coconut.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:11.160
How long is this going to continue?

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:15.120
There's no end in sight.

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:18.450
I understand. The sun is setting soon, too.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:20.200
Let's say the next game will be the last.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.330
Huh?

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:26.370
Hey, is this...

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:29.580
The last battle is a cat tower race.

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:34.620
You both start at the same time,
and the first cat to reach the end wins.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.200
Ready?

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:45.750
And so it begins. What do you think,
Commentator Maple?

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:51.370
Yes. This is another game where Coconut has
an apparent advantage due to her size.

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:53.660
But Azuki has the dexterity to compensate.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.330
This looks easy!

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:01.040
We're cats, this doesn't seem
to provide a challenge...

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:05.540
Commentator Maple?!

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:07.750
Could that be...?!

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:12.830
Ah, so you have realized...
That is not just any wall.

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.120
It is actually entirely made
of scratching post material!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:21.080
Unless you can resist the urge to touch up
your claws, you will lose a lot of time!

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.120
Truly a deterrent designed for cats.

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:37.700
Coconut and Azuki have both
overcome their primal urges!

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.750
This is only the beginning.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:44.330
What do you mean?

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:46.290
This next area is quite challenging...

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:51.750
It is called "Catfeather Bridge."

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:56.790
No cat can easily resist the urge to follow
the fluffy object with their eyes.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:17:01.620
Some may be drawn in to pounce on it
and plummet to their doom...

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.200
H-How terrifying!

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:15.330
They both take off!

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:19.330
They've closed their eyes to rush through!

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:23.700
Now the only thing left to do is to climb
this pillar up to the goal!

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:25.580
Azu-<i>nyan </i>is in the lead.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:33.290
I can't catch up to her like this...

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:40.870
If I use the cat towers on the sides,
I can overtake Azuki!

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.410
Here I come...

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.580
Yes! I passed her!

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:53.370
Now the goal is right there--

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:56.870
Coco-<i>chan</i>!

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:09.910
Idiot. Hurry up and grab the pillar!

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.200
Oh, good...

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:31.910
Thank you... for saving me.

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:37.830
You're always making extra work
for me. You never change.

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:46.160
You tried too hard, that's why you got hurt.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:50.410
But I have so much fun
playing with you, Big Sis.

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:54.000
Ugh, what a bother.

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.080
Lemme help!

00:18:58.950 --> 00:18:59.950
Oh...

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:05.080
Wh-What should I do...?

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.660
Don't touch it!

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.540
Are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:13.580
Sorry, I...

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:17.910
I'm glad you didn't get hurt.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:25.120
I was afraid you got hurt, it chilled me
to my bones. Now I've gotten shorter.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:28.910
Wait, so...

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:31.750
Back there, you were trying
to make sure I wouldn't hurt myself...?

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:37.580
Yeah, so?

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:44.000
Coco-<i>chan</i>! Azu-<i>nyan</i>!

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.500
Are you both okay?

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:50.250
I'm fine, Azuki saved me.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:54.120
It wouldn't be fun beating someone
who wipes out during the race!

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:59.160
But we still haven't decided who won.

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:02.500
Well, how about for today,
we just say it's a tie.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:06.330
Yeah. I'm tired. Let's go back and eat.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.950
Huh? What's that all about?

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:11.000
Maybe they got it out of
their system with exercise.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.250
Seems so...

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.080
Chocola is hungry, too!

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.700
Okay, let's go home, then.

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:24.700
Let's go, Nuts.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:26.950
Wait up, Big Sis!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:31.450
Nuts-<i>chan</i>, did you just call Azuki "Big Sis"?

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:32.700
N-No, I...

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:35.290
I didn't say that to Azuki, I...

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:36.290
Yes, yes.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:38.200
I said, it's not what you think!

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.750
Reminds me of old times, right?

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:41.830
Right!

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:44.750
C-Cut it out, all of you!

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:46.450
Aren't you happy, Azu-<i>nyan</i>?

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:48.700
Don't be shy, both of you.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:54.410
That's not what that was!

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.370
Did Coconut and Azuki take off already?

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:04.160
Yes, they left early--
not a lot of customers today.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:07.540
They wanted to go shopping
together on their way back.

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:12.660
Huh. I guess they're really close after all.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:17.500
Got it! This is your new bowl, Azuki!

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.250
Let's see...

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.950
What? Do you expect me to use that?

